# Steps for encrypting a dir or a file

1. Make a FS for containing the file/dir

   ```sh
   dd if=/dev/zero of=ext4.img bs=1M count=4096
   mkfs.ext4 ext4.img
   mkdir mnt
   mount -t ext4 ext4.img mnt
   ```
2. Prepare a filesystem for use with fscrypt
   
   ```sh
   fscrypt setup mnt
   fscrypt encrypt mnt  #Enable FS encryption for mnt
   ```

3. Use it

   ```sh
   cp -a secrete.dir mnt
   fscrypt lock/unlock mnt/secrete.dir 
   ```
